// The 14 MB gta_sa.exe replaces many instructions with a jump to a small stub (they sit between 0x401000 and 0x40A4D8).
// A stub hides the address of a global by adding two values, and one of them is read straight out of the exe's code
// (usually the rel32 of another thunk jump). Hooks overwrite the first bytes of a function, which changes those
// bytes; the stub then computes a wrong pointer and the process crashes far away from the hook.
// The table was generated by decoding the whole stub range; each row is one such read.
struct CodeConstantRead {
    uint32 InstructionOperand; // Address of the disp32 operand inside the stub
    uint32 CodeAddress;        // Code address that the operand points at
    uint32 OriginalValue;      // The 4 bytes stored at CodeAddress in the unmodified exe
};

